> the rest of the game.  Sure one can avoid Sokoban, I usually do.  But the 
> fact is, it doesn't really fit with the whole dungeon idea and reminds me a 
> lot more of Zelda than anything else, because it's non-random and tedious.

There are other areas of the game that are non-random. Ludios comes to 
mind, the quest levels, Vlad's tower. I agree that it's different from 
the rest of the game, and more so than Ludios or the quest. It doesn't 
appeal to everyone, but neither do some other parts of the game. As for 
not fitting with the rest of the game, I don't agree. There are still 
all the elements of nethack (except for diagonal movement between 
boulders and some other nuances). You can still use a lit of 
inventiveness like you can in the rest of the game. This inventiveness 
is somewhat limited by the special rules with regard to boulders and 
pits, and maybe those should be changed somewhat to please players who 
want to do Sokoban 'differently'. But I think it does fit with the rest 
of the game.

> Earlier this preference was compared to a dislike of pets and I feel this 
